    <ferc:DeliveryRevenues id="f-838" contextRef="c-01" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">0</ferc:DeliveryRevenues>
    <ferc:GatheringRevenues id="f-839" contextRef="c-01" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">0</ferc:GatheringRevenues>
    <ferc:IncidentalRevenue id="f-840" contextRef="c-01" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">0</ferc:IncidentalRevenue>
    <ferc:RentalRevenue id="f-841" contextRef="c-01" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">0</ferc:RentalRevenue>
    <ferc:StorageAndDemurrageRevenue id="f-842" contextRef="c-01" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">0</ferc:StorageAndDemurrageRevenue>
    <ferc:GatheringTrunkAndDeliveryRevenues id="f-844" contextRef="c-135" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">0</ferc:GatheringTrunkAndDeliveryRevenues>
    <ferc:GatheringTrunkAndDeliveryRevenues id="f-845" contextRef="c-134" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">6023155</ferc:GatheringTrunkAndDeliveryRevenues>
    <ferc:TrunkRevenues id="f-846" contextRef="c-134" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">6023155</ferc:TrunkRevenues>
    <ferc:GatheringTrunkAndDeliveryRevenues id="f-848" contextRef="c-02" unitRef="u-03" decimals="0">6023155</ferc:GatheringTrunkAndDeliveryRevenues>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-850" contextRef="c-02">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Organization.&lt;/b&gt; ET Sabina Pipeline, LLC (&amp;quot;Sabina&amp;quot;) is a Texas limited liability company. Sabina is an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;). Sabina has a 100% sole member interest in Gulf Coast/Products GP Holdings LLC (&amp;quot;Holdings&amp;quot;) and a 99% limited partnership interest in Buckeye Products Pipe Line, L.P. and Gulf Coast Pipe Line, L.P. with Holdings having an 1% general partner interest in both companies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Operations.&lt;/b&gt; Sabina is a 61-mile long, 8-inch pipeline that was placed into service in December 2024. Sabina transports natural gas liquids (&amp;quot;NGL&amp;quot;) from Mont Belvieu, Texas, to Energy Transfer's Nederland Terminal in Jefferson County, Texas, and other domestic markets in the region.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Regulation.&lt;/b&gt; Sabina's NGL transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;) and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Basis of Presentation.&lt;/b&gt; The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are : (1) subsidiaries are reflected on the equity method whereas GAAP requires that all majority-owned subsidiaries be consolidated, (2) property, plant and equipment and related depreciation are reported in accordance with FERC methodology and (3) the classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE B - SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES AND OTHER MATTERS:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period. Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Sabina capitalizes expenditures related to property, plant and equipment that have a useful life greater than one year for (1) assets purchased or constructed; (2) existing assets that are replaced or improved; or (3) land regardless of cost. During construction, Sabina capitalizes direct costs, such as labor, materials, and other costs such as overhead. Sabina records property, plant and equipment at its original cost. Sabina computes depreciation expense on a composite straight-line method at the FERC authorized rates based on the expected economic lives of the various classes of assets. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Accounts receivable are carried at the amount owed by customers less an allowance for credit losses, if deemed necessary. Sabina evaluates the collectability of accounts receivable based on review of a specific customer's ability to meet its financial obligation or as a result of changes in the overall aging of accounts receivable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Sabina's allowance for credit losses was not material as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Contract Balances with Customers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Sabina satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers. The timing of performance may differ from the timing that the associated consideration is received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract liability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Sabina recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes Sabina's fulfillment of the performance obligations. Certain contracts contain provisions requiring customers to pay a fixed fee for services, but allow customers to apply such fees against services to be provided at a future point in time. These amounts are reflected as deferred revenue until the customer applies the deficiency fees to services provided or becomes unable to use the fees as payment for future services due to expiration of the contractual period the fees can be applied or physical inability of the customer to utilize the fees due to capacity constraints.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Performance Obligations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;At contract inception, Sabina assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service that is distinct. Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Sabina generally does not own the NGL that it transports or stores.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Sabina is a limited liability company that has elected to be treated as a partnership for income tax purposes. Accordingly, the tax effects of Sabina's activities generally accrue to its members.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style="text-decoration: underline"&gt;Environmental Remediation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Sabina accrues environmental remediation costs for work at identified sites where an assessment has indicated that cleanup costs are probable and reasonably estimable. Such accruals are undiscounted and are based on currently available information, estimated timing of remedial actions and related inflation assumptions, existing technology and presently enacted laws and regulations. If a range of probable environmental cleanup costs exists for an identified site, the minimum of the range is accrued unless some other point or points in the range are more likely, in which case the most likely amount in this range is accrued. As of December 31, 2025 and 2024, there were no amounts accrued for future environmental expenditures.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE C - REGULATORY MATTER:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;On February 28, 2025, Sabina filed a depreciation study (Docket No. DO25-15-000) requesting approval of initial depreciation rates to be effective January 1, 2025. On July 18, 2025, Sabina received approval from FERC of initial depreciation rates to be effective January 1, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;b&gt;NOTE D - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Accrued capital expenditures as of December 31, 2025 and 2024 were $0.3 million and $4.4 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Non-cash contributions of net affiliated company payable during the twelve months ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 were $23.1 million and $12.2 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;Non-cash contribution of carrier and non-carrier property during the twelve months ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 were nil and $180.2 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 12pt"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
